body:
I did some adjustments in `AHashMap` which seemed to have increased performance in some situations.

### Removed the `_elements` check from `_lookup_idx_with_hash()`
There is already a validity check of `_elements` in `_lookup_idx()`, so by having it in `lookup_idx_with_hash()` too means double check.

This affects every function of `AHashMap` that uses `_lookup_idx()`: `get()`, `getptr()`, `has()`, `erase()`, `replace_key()`, `find()`, `const &operator[]` and `get_index()`.

Checks were added where `_lookup_idx_with_hash()` are called outside `_lookup_idx()`.

Consequently, this makes most `AHashMap` lookup calls in pair with `HashMap`. `_lookup_idx_with_hash()` pretty much becomes `AHashMap`'s version of `HashMap::_lookup_idx_unchecked()`.

### Removed the `unlikely` conditions from `AHashMap` lookups.
Simply because the benchmarks below over the change above on my end showed it was slightly faster.

### More versions of `_lookup_idx()` to remove the need of declaring a meta index
Some meta index declarations exist for the sole purpose of providing a value for `_lookup_idx()` to handle.

On my end, duplicating code to avoid handling a meta index resulted in faster execution.

## Benchmarks

<details>
<summary><strong>PC specs</strong></summary>
<ul>
<li><strong>CPU</strong>: Intel Core i5-11400H 2.70GHz</li>
<li><strong>GPU</strong>: NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1650</li>
<li><strong>RAM</strong>: 16GB (2x8 DDR4-3200) </li>
<li><strong>OS</strong>: Linux (CachyOS) </li>
</ul>
</details>

<details>
<summary><strong>Benchmark file</strong></summary>
<br>

```cpp
#include <chrono>
#include <cstdio>

#include "core/templates/a_hash_map.h"

#undef WARN_VERBOSE
#define WARN_VERBOSE ()

template <bool p_ensure_zero>
void *Memory::alloc_static(size_t p_bytes, bool p_pad_align) {
	void *mem;
	if constexpr (p_ensure_zero) {
		mem = calloc(1, p_bytes);
	} else {
		mem = malloc(p_bytes);
	}
	return mem;
}

void *Memory::realloc_static(void *p_memory, size_t p_bytes, bool p_pad_align) {
	if (p_memory == nullptr) {
		return alloc_static<false>(p_bytes, p_pad_align);
	}

	return realloc(p_memory, p_bytes);
}

void Memory::free_static(void *p_memory, bool p_pad_align) {
	if (p_memory) {
		free(p_memory);
	}
}


static void get(AHashMap<uint32_t, int32_t> &map) {
	printf("Benchmarking non-const get\n");
	auto start = std::chrono::system_clock::now();
	for (int i = 0; i < 50000000; i++) {
		int32_t v = map.get(i);
	}
	auto end = std::chrono::system_clock::now();
	std::chrono::duration<double> elapsed_seconds = end - start;
	printf("%f\n", elapsed_seconds);
}

void getptr(AHashMap<uint32_t, int32_t> &map) {
	printf("Benchmarking getptr\n");
	auto start = std::chrono::system_clock::now();
	for (int i = 0; i < 50000000; i++) {
		int32_t *v = map.getptr(i);
	}
	auto end = std::chrono::system_clock::now();
	std::chrono::duration<double> elapsed_seconds = end - start;
	printf("%f\n", elapsed_seconds);
}

void has(AHashMap<uint32_t, int32_t> &map) {
	printf("Benchmarking has\n");
	auto start = std::chrono::system_clock::now();
	for (int i = 0; i < 50000000; i++) {
		bool has = map.has(i);
	}
	auto end = std::chrono::system_clock::now();
	std::chrono::duration<double> elapsed_seconds = end - start;
	printf("%f\n", elapsed_seconds);
}

void constiterator_find(AHashMap<uint32_t, int32_t> &map) {
	printf("Benchmarking constiterator_find\n");
	auto start = std::chrono::system_clock::now();
	for (int i = 0; i < 50000000; i++) {
		AHashMap<uint32_t, int32_t>::ConstIterator it = map.find(i);
	}
	auto end = std::chrono::system_clock::now();
	std::chrono::duration<double> elapsed_seconds = end - start;
	printf("%f\n", elapsed_seconds);
}

void iterator_find(AHashMap<uint32_t, int32_t> &map) {
	printf("Benchmarking iterator_find\n");
	auto start = std::chrono::system_clock::now();
	for (int i = 0; i < 50000000; i++) {
		AHashMap<uint32_t, int32_t>::Iterator it = map.find(i);
	}
	auto end = std::chrono::system_clock::now();
	std::chrono::duration<double> elapsed_seconds = end - start;
	printf("%f\n", elapsed_seconds);
}



int main() {
	AHashMap<uint32_t, int32_t> map;
	map.reserve(50000000);
	for (int i = 0; i < 50000000; i++) {
		map.insert_new(i, i * 2);
	}

	// Filled runs
	printf("Benchmark case: filled maps\n");
	get(map);
	getptr(map);
	has(map);
	constiterator_find(map);
	iterator_find(map);

	// Empty runs
	map.reset();
	printf("Benchmark case: empty maps\n");
	getptr(map);
	has(map);
	constiterator_find(map);
	iterator_find(map);
	return 0;
}

```

</details>

The command to compile it is something like `g++ ahm_bench.cpp -o3 -lmimalloc -I ./godottest -I ./godot/platform/linuxbsd/ -o ahm_bench`

Might be slightly inaccurate since I couldn't find a way to use Godot's own allocator from outside like this. Hence why I used a high perfomance allocator like `mimalloc`.

